    <Action Name="Mapping" Id="{edab1274-6099-41da-a10c-63392ff253a8}">
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[// ============================================================================
// FG_04 twin <-> PLCSIM Advanced process image.
//
// Addresses: Siemens/_data/PLCTags_FG04.xlsx.
//
// The press and its verdict. Y_AxisZ is a double solenoid so that an abort
// mid-stroke leaves it where it is instead of letting a spring drive it further
// into the part - which is why the retract coil below has to be driven and not
// left to a spring that does not exist.
// ============================================================================

// --- Y_AxisZ - double solenoid, both coils and both limits ------------------
// InHome %I401.0 and HomePos %Q401.0 are BOTH NEW in this revision of the table.
// Before them the press had no way back: it reported only the bottom limit and
// the retract coil did not exist, so once bExtend dropped the twin cylinder held
// its extended position for ever.
GVL_PLC.Inputs.I401.0	:= Y_AxisZ.bRetracted;
GVL_PLC.Inputs.I401.1	:= Y_AxisZ.bExtended;
Y_AxisZ.bRetract	:= GVL_PLC.Outputs.Q401.0;
Y_AxisZ.bExtend	:= GVL_PLC.Outputs.Q401.1;

// TODO: NO ADDRESS IN PLCTags_FG04.xlsx for B_NIO (FB_SensorBinary).
// B_NIO IS NOT A SENSOR READING, it is a VERDICT: the twin's seating sensor is
// not a PLC symbol at all - it feeds PartPressDetector inside Unity, which
// publishes the conclusion here as one bit. Active means the press bottomed with
// nothing correctly seated, and it is only meaningful at the bottom limit with
// the hold expired. Without it FG_04 presses and never judges.
//   GVL_PLC.Inputs.I<n>.<b> := B_NIO.bValue;]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Action>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>